        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10577181?u=bb5932e9d514de100eb85b8d8ae8dce0e5593b2c&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">Add <code class=\"notranslate\">#[repr(_, open)]</code> on field-less (C-style) enums to allow the enum to contain unknown variants, which enables using the enum directly in FFI.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Enums with the <code class=\"notranslate\">open</code> modifier cannot be matched on exhaustively without the use of a wildcard arm. This feature is similar but distinct from the <code class=\"notranslate\">#[non_exhaustive]</code> attribute, since it works on an ABI level and applies in the defining module as well.</p>\n<hr>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Based on <a class=\"user-mention notranslate\" data-hovercard-type=\"user\" data-hovercard-url=\"/users/thomcc/hovercard\" data-octo-click=\"hovercard-link-click\" data-octo-dimensions=\"link_type:self\" href=\"https://github.com/thomcc\">@thomcc</a>'s <a href=\"https://gist.github.com/thomcc/ddd4b76c050ad7f9dfbcc68752d2f105\">initial work on a similar RFC</a>. This kind of functionality has also been discussed in the past <a href=\"https://internals.rust-lang.org/t/relaxed-discriminant-rules-for-non-exhaustive-abi-safe-enums/15987\" rel=\"nofollow\">on the internals forum</a>, more recently <a href=\"https://rust-lang.zulipchat.com/#narrow/channel/213817-t-lang/topic/Design.20for.20an.20.22enum.20with.20unknown.20variants.22.20feature\" rel=\"nofollow\">on Zulip</a> and possibly many more times before that.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Pretty sure this is <code class=\"notranslate\">T-lang</code> purview:<br>\n<a class=\"user-mention notranslate\" data-hovercard-type=\"user\" data-hovercard-url=\"/users/rustbot/hovercard\" data-octo-click=\"hovercard-link-click\" data-octo-dimensions=\"link_type:self\" href=\"https://github.com/rustbot\">@rustbot</a> label T-lang</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><strong>Please try to create inline comments for discussions to keep this RFC manageable for me.</strong></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a href=\"https://github.com/madsmtm/rfcs/blob/enum-repr-no-niches/text/3803-enum-repr-open.md\">Rendered</a>.</p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/rust-lang/rfcs/pull/3803",
            "title": "RFC: Allow making enums usable in FFI",
            "date_modified": "2025-05-12T05:24:00.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-04-21T20:36:15.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "madsmtm",
                "url": "https://github.com/madsmtm"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19656993?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">This RFC proposes adding ergonomic <code class=\"notranslate\">input!</code>, <code class=\"notranslate\">inputln!</code> and may <code class=\"notranslate\">try_input!</code> macros to Rust for reading user input, inspired by Python’s <code class=\"notranslate\">input()</code>.<br>\nThese macros simplify input handling, improve beginner experience, and provide clear error handling for EOF, parse, and I/O errors.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The goal is to make Rust more approachable for newcomers and teaching.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Previous discussions:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><a href=\"https://internals.rust-lang.org/t/pre-rfc-input-macro/527\" rel=\"nofollow\">Pre-RFC: input! macro | forum internals.rust-lang.org</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/rust-lang/rfcs/pull/67\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/rust-lang/rfcs/pull/67/hovercard\">User-friendly input macros #67</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/rust-lang/rfcs/issues/768\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/rust-lang/rfcs/issues/768/hovercard\">Simplify Standard Input (Issue #768)</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/rust-lang/rfcs/issues/1142\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/rust-lang/rfcs/issues/1142/hovercard\">New API for easier value reading from stdin #1142</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://internals.rust-lang.org/t/add-plain-simple-way-in-the-standard-library-for-reading-values-from-stdin/10846\" rel=\"nofollow\">Add plain-simple way (in the standard library) for reading values from <code class=\"notranslate\">stdin</code>? | forum internals.rust-lang.org</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/pull/75435\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/rust-lang/rust/pull/75435/hovercard\">Add <code class=\"notranslate\">std::io::input</code> simple input function. rust#75435</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/rust-lang/rfcs/pull/3183\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/rust-lang/rfcs/pull/3183/hovercard\">[Draft] RFC: Console Input Simplified #3183</a> (related RFC that additionally proposes scan macros)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/rust-lang/rfcs/pull/3196\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/rust-lang/rfcs/pull/3196/hovercard\">RFC: Add std::io::inputln() #3196</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This RFC is a compilation of comments and feedback provided on previous RFCs, especially RFC <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"1054688416\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/rust-lang/rfcs/issues/3196\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/rust-lang/rfcs/pull/3196/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/rust-lang/rfcs/pull/3196\">#3196</a> .</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a href=\"https://github.com/Phosphorus-M/rfcs/blob/input-utilities/text/0000-input-macros.md\">Rendered</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/rust-lang/rfcs/pull/3799",
            "title": "RFC: input macros",
            "date_modified": "2025-06-13T11:37:50.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-04-19T05:00:28.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "Phosphorus-M",
                "url": "https://github.com/Phosphorus-M"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3161395?u=ecb2aa155dbb36751ff120968e29ac87f076ad1a&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">About as simple as it gets.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a href=\"https://github.com/jhpratt/rfcs/blob/cfg-logical-ops/text/0000-cfg-logical-ops.md\">Rendered</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/rust-lang/rfcs/pull/3796",
            "title": "Allow `&&`, `||`, and `!` in `cfg`",
            "date_modified": "2025-07-02T02:27:29.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-03-30T22:48:29.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "jhpratt",
                "url": "https://github.com/jhpratt"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23638587?u=6d1f4ed9b2481fd4af374eb927f9a73602c53ba5&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\"><a href=\"https://github.com/jyn514/rfcs/blob/crate-attr/text/3791-crate-attr.md\">Rendered</a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">cc <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"2905664297\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/issues/138287\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/rust-lang/rust/issues/138287/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/issues/138287\">rust-lang/rust#138287</a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Differences from the current nightly implementation (note that this section is non-normative):</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><code class=\"notranslate\">-A -W -D -F</code> become aliases for <code class=\"notranslate\">crate-attr</code></li>\n<li>Attributes are prepended, not appended.</li>\n<li>Everything about how this interacts with doctests (see <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"2923808363\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/rust-lang/rfcs/issues/3791\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/rust-lang/rfcs/pull/3791/hovercard?comment_id=1999037718&amp;comment_type=review_comment\" href=\"https://github.com/rust-lang/rfcs/pull/3791#discussion_r1999037718\">#3791 (comment)</a>)</li>\n<li>The attribute shares the same Span as the crate root. In particular <code class=\"notranslate\">file!</code> behaves properly now and the edition is no longer always 2015.</li>\n</ul>",
            "url": "https://github.com/rust-lang/rfcs/pull/3791",
            "title": "RFC: `--crate-attr`",
            "date_modified": "2025-06-27T16:39:53.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-03-17T05:38:21.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "jyn514",
                "url": "https://github.com/jyn514"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1464942?u=0d7b571220d08172a442dbcafbe5d3dd3b45c786&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">The example in the API conventions (in imperative) contradicts the text (use third person). This PR corrects the example to fit the text description.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a href=\"https://github.com/vigna/rfcs/blob/fix_third_person/text/0505-api-comment-conventions.md\">Rendered</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/rust-lang/rfcs/pull/3787",
            "title": "Make examples coherent with text",
            "date_modified": "2025-03-10T08:39:46.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-03-07T10:44:26.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "vigna",
                "url": "https://github.com/vigna"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9914262?u=6d397d57ea18944924ce4d9c107b7dad87ff0c0e&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">The <code class=\"notranslate\">std::num::NonZero&lt;T&gt;</code> type allows non-zero integer semantics to be clearly expressed. Yet this<br>\ntype is only seamlessly usable if all APIs with non-zero semantics use this type, due to required<br>\nto/from conversion at any API boundary that differs in its use of <code class=\"notranslate\">NonZero</code>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The burden of these conversions is especially heavy in tests and examples. This RFC proposes new<br>\ncoercions to facilitate implicit conversion to <code class=\"notranslate\">NonZero</code> from integral constants, simplifying usage<br>\nin tests and examples, where succinctness and readability are paramount.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a href=\"https://github.com/sandersaares/rust-lang-rfcs/blob/u/sasaares/const-nonzero-ergonomics/text/3786-const-nonzero-ergonomics.md\">Rendered</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/rust-lang/rfcs/pull/3786",
            "title": "RFC: const ergonomics for NonZero<T>",
            "date_modified": "2025-06-16T05:23:43.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-03-07T09:22:17.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "sandersaares",
                "url": "https://github.com/sandersaares"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63151578?u=0a831ef01c1b17a592d62367cce371f36262f66b&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">This RFC proposes a mechanism for crates to define default bounds on generics. By specifying these defaults at the crate level we can reduce the need for verbose and repetitive <code class=\"notranslate\">?Trait</code> annotations while maintaining backward compatibility and enabling future language evolution.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">It is targeted at supporting migrations from default being <code class=\"notranslate\">Trait</code> to <code class=\"notranslate\">?Trait</code>, where <code class=\"notranslate\">Trait</code> represents some assumption that is present everywhere but is not really exercised a lot, such as <code class=\"notranslate\">Forget</code>, <code class=\"notranslate\">size = stride</code> etc. Features like <a href=\"https://github.com/rust-lang/rfcs/pull/2984\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/rust-lang/rfcs/pull/2984/hovercard\"><code class=\"notranslate\">DynSized</code></a>, as well as <a href=\"https://github.com/rust-lang/rfcs/pull/1861\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/rust-lang/rfcs/pull/1861/hovercard\"><code class=\"notranslate\">extern types</code></a>, are out of the scope of this RFC, because it does not fit into this category. <code class=\"notranslate\">DynSized</code> is not retracting mostly unexercised assumptions in order to make it <code class=\"notranslate\">?DynSized</code> the default.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Primary use case is <a href=\"https://github.com/rust-lang/rfcs/pull/3782\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/rust-lang/rfcs/pull/3782/hovercard\"><code class=\"notranslate\">Forget</code> marker trait</a>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a href=\"https://github.com/Ddystopia/rfcs/blob/local-default-bounds/text/0000-local-default-generic-bounds.md\">Rendered</a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a href=\"https://internals.rust-lang.org/t/pre-rfc-local-default-bounds/22453\" rel=\"nofollow\">Pre-RFC thread</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/rust-lang/rfcs/pull/3783",
            "title": "Local Default Bounds to assist `Forget` and other `?Trait`.",
            "date_modified": "2025-05-22T08:26:19.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-03-01T13:19:44.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "Ddystopia",
                "url": "https://github.com/Ddystopia"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63151578?u=0a831ef01c1b17a592d62367cce371f36262f66b&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">Add a <code class=\"notranslate\">Forget</code> marker trait indicating whether it is safe to skip the destructor before the value of a type exits the scope and basic utilities to work with <code class=\"notranslate\">!Forget</code> types. Introduce a seamless migration route for the standard library and ecosystem.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a href=\"https://github.com/Ddystopia/rfcs/blob/forget-marker-trait/text/0000-forget-marker-trait.md\">Rendered</a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a href=\"https://internals.rust-lang.org/t/pre-rfc-forget-marker-trait/22456\" rel=\"nofollow\">Pre-RFC thread</a></p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Unresolved questions</h3>\n<ul class=\"contains-task-list\">\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Incomplete task\"> Unsafe guarantee that <code class=\"notranslate\">!Forget</code> gives to the <code class=\"notranslate\">unsafe</code> code is already fulfilled for all <code class=\"notranslate\">'static</code> types. Because of that, it doesn't really make a lot of sense to have <code class=\"notranslate\">!Forget + 'static</code>, it is still sound to <code class=\"notranslate\">mem::forget</code> that type. Should we force <code class=\"notranslate\">impl&lt;T: 'static&gt; Forget for T</code> then? Won't that impl create some unexpected problems?</li>\n</ul>",
            "url": "https://github.com/rust-lang/rfcs/pull/3782",
            "title": "`Forget` marker trait",
            "date_modified": "2025-07-01T06:52:46.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-03-01T13:16:13.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "Ddystopia",
                "url": "https://github.com/Ddystopia"
            }
        }
    ]
}